===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause a [[#Noun|short circuit]] in.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To undergo a [[#Noun|short circuit]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|by extension}} To force [[termination]] of an ongoing process before its natural conclusion, by [[bypass]]ing one or more [[intermediary]] steps.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1998|author=Catherine Nickerson|title=The Web of Iniquity
|passage=[H]is temporarily successful attempt to smear Redfield is an effort to '''short-circuit''' the narrative into premature and mistaken resolution.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2002|author=Jim Kasper|title=Short Cycle Selling: Beating Your Competitors in the Sales Race
|passage=You do not need to follow your entire sales cycle if the customer wants to '''short-circuit''' it for you.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2003|author=Gina Hens-Piazza|title=Nameless, Blameless, and Without Shame: Two Cannibal Mothers Before a King
|passage=My mother, determined to '''short-circuit''' my outcry, would match my objections by pointing out an inherent reward for doing such work.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|by extension}} To [[impede]] or [[disrupt]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2016-11-28|author=Mike Vorkunov|title=Despite Flash of Rose’s Prime, Knicks Are Dazed by Westbrook and Thunder|journal=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/28/sports/basketball/new-york-knicks-oklahoma-city-thunder.html|passage=At times, the Knicks’ offense looked '''short-circuited'''. Anthony, despite his cold hand, kept shooting. / “They all feel good, to be honest with you,” Anthony said. “It wasn’t long, it wasn’t short, they were bouncing off the rim, they were chippers, the same shot I hit all the time so I can’t stop taking my shots.”}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|computing}} To terminate a [[loop]] before the declared termination condition is met, or a [[conditional]] before all conditions have been tested for.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2002|author=Paul Kimmel|title=Visual Basic.Net Unleashed
|passage=For example, to '''short-circuit''' the "LoggedIn()" or "LogIn()" "if" conditional, replace the "Or" with "OrElse" and the statement is interpreted to mean "if not logged in, then log in".}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2002|author=Jose Mojico|title=C# and VB.NET Conversion Pocket Reference
|passage=If you would like to '''short-circuit''', you must replace "And" with the "AndAlso" keyword and "Or" with the "OrElse" keyword, as follows....}}
#* '''2006:''' Jay Hillard &amp; Stephen Teilhet, ''C# Cookbook''
#*: The "Demand" is done to ensure that you have indeed been granted this permission before using the "Assert" to '''short-circuit''' the stackwalk.

